The team will approve a release matrix specifying participating clinics, appointment types, forms, languages, patient populations, 
and integration systems.

Out of Scope Work
- Replacement of existing electronic health record
- Comprehensive migration or digitization of historical medical records
- Secure clinical messaging and automated post appointment clinical follow up
- End to end insurance pre authorization submission
- Autonomous diagnosis
-  Broadened financial functions beyond balance viewing, payment, and payment reminders
- Appointment cancellation and rescheduling unless explicitly added to the scheduling requirements


Security, Privacy and Quality Requirements
The system must be designed and operated to support HIPAA obligations. Readiness includes administrative and technical safeguards.
Requirements include authorized access, sucure authentication and recovery, encryption in transit and at rest, audit records, approved retention and disposal,
secure uploads, backup and recovery procedures, and appropriate content must undergo privacy review. Payment handling must use an approved provider and a payment security approach that is documented.

The team will have measurable performance, availability, accessibility, recovery, and external service timeout requirements before tersting. 
False integratiuons will produce a status and recovery path. Staff permissions and patient access boundaries must be verified through positive/negative tests.


Acceptance Criteria

Patient Onboarding - approved forms validate and submit correctly; history is available to authorized users
Appointment Scheduling - succesful bookings reconcile with the source schedules; unavailable slots can't be double booked; reminders follow approved preferences
Automated Patient Services - displayed balances match the source system; payment success and failure are handles accordingly; repeated requests doesn't create duplicate charges
Patient Verification - authorized employees can review and record verification; unauthorized users can't access documents; additional verification and recovery scenariors are compliant
Patient Profile and Security - patients can update only permitted information; each patient sees only their own approved activity records







